1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. a3 Bxc3+ 5. bxc3 Ne7 6. Bd3 c5 7. e5 Qa5 8. Qd2
Nbc6 9. Nf3 c4 10. Be2 Qa4 11. O-O Bd7 12. Ne1 O-O-O 13. f4 $6 f5 $11 14. Qd1
Rdg8 15. Be3 Nd8 16. Qd2 h6 17. Nf3 Be8 18. Rfb1 Bh5 19. Rb4 Qd7 20. a4 Nec6
21. Rb5 b6 22. Kh1 Na5 23. Ng1 Bxe2 24. Nxe2 g5 $15 25. Qe1 Rg7 26. Qf2 Nf7 27.
Rbb1 Qe8 28. Rg1 Rhg8 29. g3 Nc6 30. Qe1 Nfd8 31. Qf2 Kb7 32. Qf3 Qg6 33. Rgb1
Kc8 34. Rg1 Kd7 35. Rab1 Qe8 36. Ra1 Nf7 37. Qf2 Kc7 38. Qf3 Nh8 39. Qf2 Qe7
40. Qf3 Ng6 41. Bd2 Kd7 42. Be3 {Whilst the position is unpleasant for White,
he has defended well, shoring up f4. Black now transfers play to the h-file.}
g4 43. Qf1 h5 44. Bf2 h4 $17 45. gxh4 Rh8 46. Rg2 Rgh7 47. Bg3 Nxh4 48. Bxh4
Rxh4 49. Ng3 Rh3 50. Qb1 Qh4 51. Nf1 Rf3 52. a5 Rb8 $2 {Fear of not much
dictated this move being played.} (52... Nxa5 $1 53. Rxa5 (53. Qb4 Kc8) 53...
bxa5 54. Qb7+ Ke8) 53. axb6 Rxb6 54. Qc1 Rb8 $2 (54... Qh6 $19) 55. Qd2 Qh6 56.
Rf2 Rxf2 57. Qxf2 a5 58. Ne3 Kc7 59. Kg1 Ra8 $17 60. Nd1 a4 61. Ne3 a3 62. Kg2
Ra4 63. Nd1 Na7 64. Qf1 Nb5 65. Nb2 axb2 66. Rxa4 Nxc3 67. Rb4 b1=Q 68. Rxb1
Nxb1 69. Qxb1 Qxf4 70. Qa1 Qe3 71. Kf1 Kb6 72. Qb2+ Kc6 73. Qa1 Qf3+ 74. Kg1
Kb5 75. c3 Qe3+ 76. Kf1 Qd3+ 77. Kg1 g3 78. Qb2+ Kc6 79. hxg3 Qxg3+ 80. Kh1
Qf3+ 81. Kh2 Qh5+ 82. Kg2 Qg5+ 83. Kf1 Kd7 84. Qb7+ Ke8 85. Qc7 Qe7 86. Qc8+
Kf7 87. Qh8 Qg5 88. Qh7+ Qg7 89. Qh5+ Qg6 90. Qh4 Qg7 91. Qh5+ Ke7 92. Qh4+ Kd7
93. Qh5 $6 {Gives Black a breather.} f4 $1 94. Qh4 $2 f3 95. Qh3 Qg2+ $1 $19
96. Qxg2 fxg2+ 97. Kxg2 Kc6 98. Kg3 Kb5 99. Kg4 Ka4 100. Kg5 Kb3 101. Kf6 Kxc3
102. Kxe6 Kxd4 103. Kd6 c3 104. e6 c2 105. e7 c1=Q 106. e8=Q {Most queen
endings with a clear extra pawn should be winning. But there is plenty of work
to be done!} Qf4+ 107. Kc6 Qf6+ 108. Kb7 Qe5 109. Qa4+ Ke3 110. Qa3+ Ke4 111.
Qb4+ d4 112. Qe1+ Kd5 113. Qd1 Qe4 114. Ka6 d3 115. Qh5+ Kd4 116. Qh8+ Qe5 (
116... Kc5 117. Qf8+ Kc4 118. Qc8+ Kb3 119. Qd8 Qc4+ 120. Kb6 Kc2) 117. Qd8+
Ke3 118. Qd7 d2 119. Qh3+ Kf2 120. Qh4+ Qg3 121. Qd4+ Ke2 122. Qe4+ Qe3 123.
Qg2+ Kd3 124. Qd5+ Qd4 125. Qb3+ Qc3 126. Qb1+ Qc2 127. Qf1+ Kc3 128. Qf6+ Kb3
129. Qb6+ Ka3 (129... Ka2 130. Qa5+ Kb3 131. Qb6+ Ka3 132. Qd6+ Ka2 133. Qd5+
Ka1 134. Qd4+ $6 Qb2 135. Qg1+ Ka2 136. Qg8+ Qb3 137. Qg2 Qd3+ 138. Kb6 Kb1 {
0-1 is the finish given by 2022 CB Mega Database}) 130. Qd6+ Ka2 131. Qd5+ Ka1
132. Qd4+ $6 Qb2 133. Qg1+ Ka2 134. Qg8+ {When the checks get more and more
"long distance", you know the end is nigh.} Qb3 135. Qg2 Qd3+ 136. Kb6 Kb1 {
Source: Darryl Johansen. Contributed by Paul Summers, 16 February 2023.} 0-1

